  "prompt": "Complete the final cumulative Fabric 1.21.4 project. Rerun the full morph and kill-feed scenarios, capture the current player UUID before the HUD kill and bind the player combat event attackerUuid to it, then implement death rewind. Generate random P/A/C player states in the test region, capture P, wait a real 61000ms with at least 1200 server ticks, change to A and C, kill the player, wait_until DeathScreen, respawn, wait_until serverPlayer.available and capture R. Use player_state_v1 relations to prove R=P and R differs from A and C, compare full inventory and selected slot, verify client/server synchronization, and prove true death/respawn. The final scenario must require two independent complete PASS runs after a Minecraft JVM restart, with different random variables and window size while keeping the same scenario id/revision/fingerprint. Do not use fixed coordinates, fixed health, snapshot_changed, screenshots or user confirmation. Build, launch and repair autonomously.",
